{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Moab</b> — I will wash their land like a pot. Behold, we have found the opposite in 'Philistia, cry out because of me' (the word [used] opposite [to its usual sense]). R. Moses the Cohen interpreted it: 'Behold, upon Edom, which is strong, I will cast my sandal; I reckon you, Philistia, that you cry out over me,' in the manner of: 'Rejoice, young man, in your youth'; 'Come to Bethel.'"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 60, :notes {0 "The phrase הפוך is understood as indicating a word used in an inverted/opposite sense; the exact reference and syntax are compressed and somewhat obscure in the original."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:32:24.977831994Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}